                                                                  7837 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     7837 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        7837 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     7837 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     7837 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            7837 1451
                                                                  7837 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           7837 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         7837 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen, Switzerland. The RRR  7837 1451
       expands from 0 to 9.718586E+3 eV. A total of               7837 1451
       2 l-values are used and 66 resonances. The resonance       7837 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              7837 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       7837 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          7837 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     7837 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    7837 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  7837 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   7837 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          7837 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       7837 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    7837 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       7837 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         7837 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 201.1 eV and           7837 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0001283 1e-4.             7837 1451
                                                                  7837 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  7837 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    7837 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    7837 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   7837 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    7837 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              7837 1451
